Alt\-X in emacs mode opens a minibuffer under the buffer that takes the
command to run. Tab completes the command, Enter runs it, and Escape,
Ctrl\-C, Ctrl\-D, or Backspace on an empty minibuffer closes it. The hint rows
list the commands that start with the text typed so far. An unknown command
does nothing. The buffer keeps its syntax highlighting.
